.TH QFW-SLURM-EPILOG 8 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-epilog \- release QPM reservations after Slurm allocation completion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-slurm-epilog
.RI [ --config " path" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-epilog
is installed as a Slurm
.B EpilogSlurmctld
program. It reads the authoritative allocation identity supplied by the
controller and calls the same typed release operation used by
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1).
.PP
The epilog logs every unresolved service result. Release failures remain in
the gateway journal for operator recovery. The program returns zero after
diagnostics because allocation termination is already in progress and a QPM
failure must not mark a healthy compute node down.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read a native client configuration other than
.IR /etc/qfw-slurm/plugin.conf .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLURM_CLUSTER_NAME
Cluster name used for the release request. Required.
.TP
.B SLURM_JOB_ID
Canonical job ID for a normal allocation. Required.
.TP
.B SLURM_HET_JOB_ID
Canonical heterogeneous job leader when Slurm supplies one.
.TP
.B SLURM_JOB_START_TIME
Optional allocation epoch.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configure the controller with an absolute path, for example:
.PP
.RS
.B EpilogSlurmctld=/usr/sbin/qfw-slurm-epilog
.RE
.PP
The native configuration must be readable by the configured Slurm controller
account. Its endpoint must identify the same gateway that handled reserve.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command returns zero after both successful and failed release attempts.
Invalid command-line syntax returns 2. Operational failures are written to
standard error and retained in the gateway journal when a reservation record
exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1),
.BR qfw-slurm-plugin.conf (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway (8)
